  "capturedAt": "2026-11-09",
  "question": "R2, rule S (new, first round): does the oracle keep a one-line Text's second row at a widening drop when its new right line sits under half a pixel past a whole pixel? Unseen setups: the short Text written on column 2 at 1280 (columns 49.515625px, so the fraction alternates by line) widened to lines 13, 14, 17, 18; at 1920 (same fractions as 1600, 160px over) to line 15; and at 1600 an empty Text moved to column 3 before it is written, widened to lines 15 and 17. Read at the drop and let go, twice (R1, R2). Gestures Probe, unsaved.",
  "rule": "S: a one-line Text widened by its east side keeps its rows at the drop when x of its new right grid line has a fractional part under 0.5 px, and falls to the rows it needs otherwise; let go always takes the rows it needs. Grid line x = line 2 + (k - 2) * pitch: 1600 100.125 and 58.78125, 1920 260.125 and 58.78125, 1280 51.1875 and 49.515625 (ours' computed grid, equal to the oracle's boxes in CAP-G4WIDTHS.json and CAP-X2W456B.json).",
  "from": "Scratch predictor of rule S. Seen: the short Text's held reads at 1600 (CAP-R2WIDEDROP a1 to a8, CAP-R2ENDLINE A to C, CAP-TEXTWIDTH7 f3, f4, f7): 17 of 18; the miss is column 3 line 15 after a move, where the move had wrapped the text to 2 lines. asBuilt: ours on main, which falls at every drop.",
  "hit": "Scored on the Text's desktop area at 'held' and 'let go' (each case's two reads must agree). A setup miss, named and not scored: the 'written' read not on its start area, or the held text not one line (textH over 30).",
